{"title":"2006 Seniors Pancyprian/2nd grade/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, that has no parallel sides, is inscribed in a circle, its sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and its sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />.\nIf the bisectors of of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/19422ac6989f4e7e0909ca59bd5b82c917359d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b04d055c571d59de3557e0a071f56586ae6224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CZB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> intersect the sides of the quadrilateral at the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec479b6af5aa92e18d2ffff40b016d7b4ddc3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K , L, M ,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> prove that\n</p><p>i)The bisectors intersect normally\n</p><p>ii)the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec479b6af5aa92e18d2ffff40b016d7b4ddc3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K , L, M ,N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> are vertices of a rhombus.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Seniors Pancyprian/2nd grade/Problem 5\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Seniors Pancyprian/2nd grade/Problem 3\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade\" title=\"2006 Seniors Pancyprian/2nd grade\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Seniors_Pancyprian/2nd_grade/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Seniors_Pancyprian_Competition\" title=\"Seniors Pancyprian C